  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "A positive number \\(x\\) has the property that \\(x\\%\\) of \\(x\\) is \\(4.\\) What is \\(x?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\)",
    "D": "\\(20\\)",
    "E": "\\(40\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Since \\(x\\%\\) means \\(x/100\\), taking \\(x\\%\\) of \\(x\\) means multiplying \\(x\\) by \\(x/100\\). Thus\n\\[\n\\frac{x}{100}\\cdot x=4,\n\\qquad\\text{so}\\qquad x^2=400.\n\\]\nThe two real numbers whose square is 400 are \\(20\\) and \\(-20\\). Because \\(x\\) is positive, \\(x=\\boxed{20}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
